ion\">,</span> <span class=\"attr\">&quot;body&quot;</span><span class=\"punctuation\">:</span> <span class=\"string\">&quot;# 📌 Introduction\\n\\nA compilation of resources and concepts related to Open Source, for self-study and note-taking.&quot;</span><span class=\"punctuation\">&#125;</span></span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<span id=\"more\"></span>\n<figure class=\"highlight json\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"punctuation\">&#123;</span><span class=\"attr\">&quot;title&quot;</span><span class=\"punctuation\">:</span> <span class=\"string\">&quot;[note] Resources on Open Source&quot;</span><span class=\"punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"attr\">&quot;body&quot;</span><span class=\"punctuation\">:</span> <span class=\"string\">&quot;# 🚀 Introduction\\n\\n# Q&amp;A\\n\\n- **What is an OSPO (Open Source Program Office)? [^ospo]**\\n- **What are the core responsibilities of an OSPO? [^ospo-core]**\\n- **What is the most important value of an OSPO?** [^ospo-value]\\n- **What is the [TODO Group](https://todogroup.org/)? [^todogroup]**\\n\\n## [^ospo]: What is an OSPO (Open Source Program Office)?\\n\\nA unit dedicated to formulating, managing, and promoting open source strategy. It is not just \\&quot;using open source software,\\&quot; but participating in the open source ecosystem in a systematic and strategic way.\\n\\n## [^ospo-core]: What are the core responsibilities of an OSPO?\\n\\nhttps://ospoglossary.todogroup.org/ospo-definition/\\n\\n| Work Area | Specific Content |\\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------ |\\n| Open Source Governance (Governance) | Establish policies for the use, review, and contribution of open source software |\\n| License Compliance (Compliance) | Manage risks of licenses such as MIT, Apache 2.0, GPL |\\n| Software Supply Chain (Security) | Promote SBOM, SCA, and open source component risk management |\\n| Open Source Contribution (Contribution) | Establish processes for employees to submit PRs and report Issues |\\n| Open Source Strategy (Strategy) | Decide which technologies are worth investing in, contributing to, or open-sourcing |\\n| Community Management (Community) | Participate in foundations, technical communities, and open source events |\\n\\n&gt; Organized by ChatGPT\\n\\n## [^ospo-value]: What is the most important value of an OSPO?\\n\\nIt can be divided into three stages.\\n\\n|          1          |          2          |         3         |\\n| :------------------: | :------------------: | :----------------: |\\n|  **Consume**  | **Contribute** |   **Lead**   |\\n| Safely and compliantly use open source | Contribute to existing open source projects | Lead projects and manage communities |\\n\\nIt is not just about managing which open source software the company uses, but about considering how to make open source a long-term technical capability, competitive advantage, and external collaboration resource for the enterprise.\\n\\n&gt; Organized by ChatGPT\\n\\n&gt; Extended topic: Beyond enterprises, what about general developers?\\n\\n&lt;!-- # 🔁 Key Takeaways --&gt;\\n\\n# 🔗 References\\n\\n&gt; To be organized; currently just collected\\n\\n- https://ospoglossary.todogroup.org/ospo-definition/\\n- https://ospobook.todogroup.org/01-chapter/\\n- https://www.linuxfoundation.org/blog/blog/is-it-time-for-an-ospo-in-your-organization\\n- https://events.linuxfoundation.org/archive/2026/open-source-summit-north-america/\\n\\n&gt; TODO\\n\\n- OSPO 101 Module 1 - Open Source Introduction: https://github.com/todogroup/ospo-career-path/tree/main/OSPO-101/module1\\n- OSPO 101 Module 2 - Open Source Business Models: https://github.com/todogroup/ospo-career-path/tree/main/OSPO-101/module2\\n- OSPO 101 Module 3 - Open Source Management &amp; Your Organization: https://github.com/todogroup/ospo-career-path/tree/main/OSPO-101/module3&quot;</span><s